<Wizard::IntroContent
  @isOptional={{true}}
  @imageAlt="Identity group and external group mapping"
  @imageCaption="Internal groups designate entities manually within Vault. External groups sync group membership based on your identity provider."
  @imageSrc={{img-path "~/groups-intro.png"}}
>
  <:description>
    Groups collect
    <strong>multiple entities under a shared identity unit</strong>, allowing policies to be assigned at a group level rather
    than individually. Each group can contain subgroups, with policies cascading down to all members.
  </:description>
  <:features>
    <Wizard::IntroContent::Feature @icon="service">
      Groups are used to
      <strong>apply shared policies across teams</strong>, mirroring existing Identity Provider (IdP) groupings.
    </Wizard::IntroContent::Feature>
    <Wizard::IntroContent::Feature @icon="database">
      Groups are
      <strong>scoped to the namespace where they are created.</strong>
      They extend down to child namespaces, but are not applied cluster-wide by default.
    </Wizard::IntroContent::Feature>
    <Wizard::IntroContent::Feature @icon="org">
      Groups come in two forms: internal group membership is managed and dictated within Vault; external group membership is
      directly mirrors and syncs membership from your identity provider.
    </Wizard::IntroContent::Feature>
  </:features>
</Wizard::IntroContent>